{"assessment":"The source supports the incompressible kinetic energy E_i scaling with quench duration tau_Q at two temperatures (T=10^-6 and T=1), with fitted power laws and explicit fit uncertainties. The operational definition of equilibration time is provided in the supplementary material. The control tau_Q is a linear chemical-potential ramp with dimensionless scaled units. The readout E_i is defined via the density-weighted velocity field and its incompressible component. The claims are anchored to the relevant lines, including the fit method and ensemble counts. The applicability domain [100,1000] is supported by reviewer figure evidence and the source's own fit ranges. The fast-quench deviation statement is noted as a general limitation, not part of the fitted domain. The fit uncertainty convention is source_unspecified, and the numeric values are preserved. The card is case_authoring_ready true.","case_authoring_ready":true,"claims":[{"anchors":[{"line_end":443,"line_start":443,"support":"Fitted power law: E_i = (19.774 ± 5.010) × 10^4 τ_Q^{-0.971 ± 0.052} for panel (a)."},{"line_end":445,"line_start":445,"support":"For all fits with exact independent variables, we use weighted least squares with weights given by the inverse variances."},{"line_end":390,"line_start":390,"support":"Each data point is averaged over (a) R=2000 stochastic realizations."}],"applicability":"The fitted power law is reported for quench durations tau_Q in [100, 1000] at temperature T=10^-6.","claim_id":"ei_scaling_lowT","control_domains":[{"allowed_values":[],"anchors":[{"line_end":1112,"line_start":1110,"support":"Both fitted curve segments visibly cover the labeled quench-duration interval from tau_Q=10^2 through tau_Q=10^3."}],"control_name":"tau_Q","domain_kind":"continuous_interval","domain_statement":"The fitted E_i curve for T=10^-6 covers the quench-duration interval from 10^2 to 10^3.","maximum":1000.0,"minimum":100.0}],"control_names":["tau_Q"],"depends_on":[],"fixed_condition_ids":["simulation_parameters_common","equilibration_time_definition","temperature_lowT"],"mechanism_ids":["kzm_ei_scaling"],"oracle_outputs":{"E_i":{"args":[{"param":"ei_amplitude_lowT"},{"args":[{"var":"tau_Q"},{"param":"ei_exponent_lowT"}],"op":"power"}],"op":"multiply"}},"quantitative_form":"E_i = (19.774 ± 5.010) × 10^4 * tau_Q^(-0.971 ± 0.052)","readout_names":["E_i"],"statement":"At temperature T=10^-6, the total incompressible kinetic energy at equilibration time scales with quench duration as E_i = (19.774 ± 5.010) × 10^4 τ_Q^{-0.971 ± 0.052}, consistent with the predicted τ_Q^{-1} scaling.","statistical_basis":"Weighted least squares with weights given by the inverse variances, as stated for all fits with exact independent variables. Data averaged over R=2000 stochastic realizations.","uncertainty":"Fit amplitude uncertainty +/- 5.010e4 and exponent uncertainty +/- 0.052, with convention source_unspecified. Data error bars denote 1 standard deviation."},{"anchors":[{"line_end":443,"line_start":443,"support":"Fitted power law: E_i = (9.543 ± 2.951) × 10^4 τ_Q^{-0.935 ± 0.068} in panel (b)."},{"line_end":445,"line_start":445,"support":"For all fits with exact independent variables, we use weighted least squares with weights given by the inverse variances."},{"line_end":390,"line_start":390,"support":"Each data point is averaged over (b) R=1000 stochastic realizations."}],"applicability":"The fitted power law is reported for quench durations tau_Q in [100, 1000] at temperature T=1.","claim_id":"ei_scaling_T1","control_domains":[{"allowed_values":[],"anchors":[{"line_end":1112,"line_start":1110,"support":"Both fitted curve segments visibly cover the labeled quench-duration interval from tau_Q=10^2 through tau_Q=10^3."}],"control_name":"tau_Q","domain_kind":"continuous_interval","domain_statement":"The fitted E_i curve for T=1 covers the quench-duration interval from 10^2 to 10^3.","maximum":1000.0,"minimum":100.0}],"control_names":["tau_Q"],"depends_on":[],"fixed_condition_ids":["simulation_parameters_common","equilibration_time_definition","temperature_T1"],"mechanism_ids":["kzm_ei_scaling"],"oracle_outputs":{"E_i":{"args":[{"param":"ei_amplitude_T1"},{"args":[{"var":"tau_Q"},{"param":"ei_exponent_T1"}],"op":"power"}],"op":"multiply"}},"quantitative_form":"E_i = (9.543 ± 2.951) × 10^4 * tau_Q^(-0.935 ± 0.068)","readout_names":["E_i"],"statement":"At temperature T=1, the total incompressible kinetic energy at equilibration time scales with quench duration as E_i = (9.543 ± 2.951) × 10^4 τ_Q^{-0.935 ± 0.068}, consistent with the predicted τ_Q^{-1} scaling.","statistical_basis":"Weighted least squares with weights given by the inverse variances, as stated for all fits with exact independent variables. Data averaged over R=1000 stochastic realizations.","uncertainty":"Fit amplitude uncertainty +/- 2.951e4 and exponent uncertainty +/- 0.068, with convention source_unspecified. Data error bars denote 1 standard deviation."}],"controls":[{"allowed_values":[],"anchors":[{"line_end":157,"line_start":156,"support":"Linear quench of the chemical potential, mu(t) = mu_i + (mu_f - mu_i) t / tau_Q."},{"line_end":148,"line_start":148,"support":"Dimensionless units used throughout the manuscript."},{"line_end":1112,"line_start":1110,"support":"Both fitted curve segments visibly cover the labeled quench-duration interval from tau_Q=10^2 through tau_Q=10^3."}],"definition":"Quench duration of the linear chemical-potential ramp mu(t) = mu_i + (mu_f - mu_i) t / tau_Q, driving the system through the critical point.","domain_kind":"continuous_interval","domain_statement":"The fitted E_i curves are reported for quench durations from 10^2 to 10^3.","maximum":1000.0,"minimum":100.0,"name":"tau_Q","unit":"dimensionless (scaled units)"}],"fixed_conditions":[{"anchors":[{"line_end":460,"line_start":460,"support":"Length, time, and temperature are measured in units of l, hbar/E_sc, and E_sc/k_B."},{"line_end":507,"line_start":491,"support":"Simulations in periodic L x L box with L=30, t_r=10, mu_i=0.1, mu_f=20, g=1, gamma=0.03, T=1, epsilon_cut=2.5 mu_f."}],"condition_id":"simulation_parameters_common","statement":"Periodic L x L homogeneous box with L=30, initial chemical potential mu_i=0.1, final chemical potential mu_f=20, coupling g=1, damping gamma=0.03, energy cutoff epsilon_cut=2.5 mu_f, and relaxation time t_r=10. Length, time, and temperature are measured in units of l=sqrt(hbar^2/(m E_sc)), hbar/E_sc, and E_sc/k_B respectively."},{"anchors":[{"line_end":517,"line_start":514,"support":"The equilibration time t_eq is identified by analyzing N_C/L^2, locating the global maximum of d^2(N_C/L^2)/dt^2, and identifying the subsequent interval (t1,t2) where d^2(N_C/L^2)/dt^2 <= -Delta with Delta=10% of the maximum, then taking t_eq=t2."}],"condition_id":"equilibration_time_definition","statement":"The equilibration time t_eq is determined by analyzing N_C/L^2, locating the global maximum of its second derivative, then identifying the subsequent interval (t1,t2) where the second derivative is <= -Delta with Delta=10% of that maximum, and setting t_eq=t2."},{"anchors":[{"line_end":390,"line_start":390,"support":"Panels (a) and (b) show the incompressible kinetic energy E_i at the equilibration time for various quench times tau_Q at temperature T = 10^-6 and T = 1, respectively."},{"line_end":148,"line_start":148,"support":"Dimensionless units used throughout the manuscript."}],"condition_id":"temperature_lowT","statement":"Temperature T = 10^-6 (dimensionless scaled units)."},{"anchors":[{"line_end":390,"line_start":390,"support":"Panels (a) and (b) show the incompressible kinetic energy E_i at the equilibration time for various quench times tau_Q at temperature T = 10^-6 and T = 1, respectively."},{"line_end":148,"line_start":148,"support":"Dimensionless units used throughout the manuscript."}],"condition_id":"temperature_T1","statement":"Temperature T = 1 (dimensionless scaled units)."}],"mechanisms":[{"anchors":[{"line_end":417,"line_start":414,"support":"Equation (eq:scaling_E_i_nu_z): E_i proportional to tau_Q^{-(1+2 nu)/(1+z nu)}"},{"line_end":444,"line_start":443,"support":"Fitted power laws confirm the predicted tau_Q^{-1} behavior based on mean-field exponents nu=1/2 and z=2."}],"equations":["E_i \\propto \\tau_Q^{-(1+2\\nu)/(1+z\\nu)}","E_i = A \\tau_Q^{-\\alpha}"],"mechanism_id":"kzm_ei_scaling","parameters":[{"anchors":[{"line_end":167,"line_start":167,"support":"Using the mean-field values of the critical exponents nu = 1/2 and z = 2"}],"name":"nu_critical_exponent","role":"correlation-length critical exponent","uncertainty":"source_unspecified","unit":"dimensionless","value":0.5},{"anchors":[{"line_end":167,"line_start":167,"support":"Using the mean-field values of the critical exponents nu = 1/2 and z = 2"}],"name":"z_dynamic_exponent","role":"dynamic critical exponent","uncertainty":"source_unspecified","unit":"dimensionless","value":2.0},{"anchors":[{"line_end":443,"line_start":443,"support":"E_i = (19.774 ± 5.010) × 10^4 τ_Q^{-0.971 ± 0.052} for panel (a)"}],"name":"ei_amplitude_lowT","role":"amplitude of the fitted power law for E_i at T=10^-6","uncertainty":"source_unspecified: +/- 5.010e4","unit":"dimensionless (scaled units)","value":197740.0},{"anchors":[{"line_end":443,"line_start":443,"support":"E_i = (19.774 ± 5.010) × 10^4 τ_Q^{-0.971 ± 0.052} for panel (a)"}],"name":"ei_exponent_lowT","role":"exponent of the fitted power law for E_i at T=10^-6","uncertainty":"source_unspecified: +/- 0.052","unit":"dimensionless","value":-0.971},{"anchors":[{"line_end":443,"line_start":443,"support":"E_i = (9.543 ± 2.951) × 10^4 τ_Q^{-0.935 ± 0.068} in panel (b)"}],"name":"ei_amplitude_T1","role":"amplitude of the fitted power law for E_i at T=1","uncertainty":"source_unspecified: +/- 2.951e4","unit":"dimensionless (scaled units)","value":95430.0},{"anchors":[{"line_end":443,"line_start":443,"support":"E_i = (9.543 ± 2.951) × 10^4 τ_Q^{-0.935 ± 0.068} in panel (b)"}],"name":"ei_exponent_T1","role":"exponent of the fitted power law for E_i at T=1","uncertainty":"source_unspecified: +/- 0.068","unit":"dimensionless","value":-0.935}],"statement":"The incompressible kinetic energy at equilibration scales as E_i proportional to tau_Q^{-(1+2 nu)/(1+z nu)}, with mean-field exponents nu=1/2 and z=2, giving E_i proportional to tau_Q^{-1}.","variable_names":["E_i","tau_Q","nu","z","A","alpha"]}],"paper_scope":"The paper establishes the Kibble-Zurek universality of the total incompressible kinetic energy E_i at equilibration time, reporting fitted power-law scalings with quench duration tau_Q at two temperatures (T=10^-6 and T=1). The separate collapse of rescaled spectra is not part of this selected cluster.","readouts":[{"anchors":[{"line_end":200,"line_start":187,"support":"Density-weighted velocity field u = |Psi_C| v, decomposition into compressible and incompressible components, and definition of E_i,c = (1/2) integral |u_i,c|^2 d^2r."},{"line_end":413,"line_start":394,"support":"E_i defined as (1/2) integral |u_i(r, t_eq)|^2 d^2r = integral_0^infinity E_i(k) dk."},{"line_end":390,"line_start":390,"support":"Each data point is averaged over (a) R=2000 and (b) R=1000 stochastic realizations. Error bars denote 1 standard deviation."},{"line_end":148,"line_start":148,"support":"Dimensionless units used throughout the manuscript."}],"definition":"Total incompressible kinetic energy at equilibration time, defined as E_i = (1/2) integral |u_i(r, t_eq)|^2 d^2r = integral_0^infinity E_i(k) dk, where u_i is the incompressible (solenoidal) component of the density-weighted velocity field u = |Psi_C| v.","name":"E_i","resolution":null,"statistic":"Ensemble average over R=2000 (T=10^-6) and R=1000 (T=1) stochastic realizations.","uncertainty":"Error bars denote 1 standard deviation.","unit":"dimensionless (scaled units)"}],"source":{"arxiv_versioned_id":"2506.21670v3","citation":"Seong-Ho Shinn, Spontaneous Quantum Turbulence in a Newborn Bose-Einstein Condensate via the Kibble-Zurek Mechanism, Physical Review Letters (2026), DOI:10.1103/b16v-hwp2","journal_doi":"10.1103/b16v-hwp2"},"source_ambiguities":[]}
